1. Nullable(String), no preprocessor.
tp	1	\N	\N	\N	\N
tp	2	1	1	1	1
tp	3	0	0	0	0
tp	4	0	0	0	0
tn	1	\N	\N	\N	\N
tn	2	0	1	1	1
tn	3	0	0	0	0
tn	4	0	0	0	0
tp NOT hasToken	[3,4]
tn NOT hasToken	[3,4]
tp NOT hasAnyTokens	[3,4]
tn NOT hasAnyTokens	[3,4]
tp NOT hasAllTokens	[3,4]
tn NOT hasAllTokens	[3,4]
tp NOT hasPhrase	[3,4]
tn NOT hasPhrase	[3,4]
tp NOT, direct read off	[3,4]
tn NOT, direct read off	[3,4]
tp IS NULL, direct read off	[1]
tn IS NULL, direct read off	[1]
tp merge()	[3,4]
tn merge()	[2,3,4]
2. Nullable(String) with a preprocessor, applied to the haystack of an analyzed index.
tp_lower	[3,4]
tn_lower	[3,4]
tp_ifnull	[1,3,4]
tn_ifnull	[1,3,4]
tp_nullif	[3]
tn_nullif	[3]
3. String and FixedString with a NULL-producing preprocessor: the predicate is not Nullable.
tp_nullif_str	[3,4]
tp_nullif_fs	[1,2]
